As an archetype, yes: process orientation vs. endpoint orientation.

A lot of male behavior is organized around getting there: solve it, win it, finish it, acquire it, climax. A lot of female behavior is more sensitive to the trajectory: anticipation, atmosphere, unfolding, attention, emotional transitions, how one moment leads into the next.

That can explain a surprising amount of mismatch in dating, sex, shopping, conversation, travel, even storytelling. One person thinks, “What are we trying to accomplish?” The other thinks, “Why are you rushing through the part that makes the accomplishment meaningful?”

But I wouldn’t make it a biological absolute. There’s huge individual overlap. The more useful formulation is:

Some people optimize for arrival; others optimize for experience.
If you only understand the destination, you can accidentally destroy the journey that makes someone want to arrive there with you.